 retail stores in the United States and Canada. The company offers oil changes; battery, bulb, and wiper replacements; tire rotations; and other maintenance services. It also operates and franchises service centers and retail locations. The company was founded in 1866 and is headquartered in Lexington, Kentucky.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Lori A. Flees | CEO, President & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $1.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 10K people. Revenue per employee of $161K ranks in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $4K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $991 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 12\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Valvoline Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $4.4B market cap on $1.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -17% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 25% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 17-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 37%.","The business throws off $38M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 2 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.41\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 5.3\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 1.7%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.9\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.06041375380405604},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (12.4% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 13% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Operating margins 15% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Valvoline (VVV) Faces Margin Pressure, Is It Still 19% Undervalued?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/retail/nyse-vvv/valvoline/news/valvoline-vvv-faces-margin-pressure-is-it-still-19-undervalu","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794554313.22,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.896,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Analysts Estimate Valvoline (VVV) to Report a Decline in Earnings: What to Look Out 