ion (15.2% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is -5, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business.","It has beaten earnings estimates by 10.6% on average."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.3%), and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insider trading is two-way: 1 purchase and 1 sale over the past year.","Shareholder yield is a modest 1.7% (1.7% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 6.6% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","Short interest is elevated at 12.4% of the float, 5.3 days to cover."],"people":["With about 10,600 employees, each generates about $161K of revenue, 0.4x the Consumer Cyclical median, and revenue has fallen 2.4% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $4K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $1.9M (12x revenue per employee)."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":48,"head":"Watch: composite 40, above the 39 line, but no margin of safety and the fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread); it becomes a buy below $27.75.","pros":["Composite 40, above the 39 line (gates 11/24)","ROIC 24.8% vs WACC 8.1%","16 analysts' mean target $42.31 (+22%)"],"cons":["Trades 6% above fair value of $32.65","Revenue shrank 6.2%/yr over 5y","Fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)","P/E 42.7x vs sector 18.8x","P/FCF 116.2x vs sector 16.7x"],"flags":[],"need":["no margin of safety","the fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)","too few checks pass (conviction 48)"],"buy_below":27.75,"vc":{"base":32.65,"base_src":"dcf","bear":17.69,"bull":55.75,"alt_median":58.69,"n_alt":2,"gap":-0.4437,"dispersion":0.0381,"level":"LOW","why":["Monte Carlo spread is wide","bull case is 3.2x the bear case"]},"med":{"pe":18.8184,"ev_ebitda":10.707,"pfcf":16.6971,"pb":2.3,"roic":0.1268,"gross_margin":0.346,"fcf_margin":0.0621,"div_yield":0.0232}},"mc_quantiles":[9.56,15.07,17.69,20.46,22.19,24.3